<Shell title="Aero · Blind Validation Challenge 01" description="Public source selection, reference-withholding protocol and honest incomplete chronology. No completed blind experimental result is claimed." path="/software/aero/evidence/benchmarks/blind-validation-01/">
<header><p class="eyebrow">EXTERNAL BENCHMARK / CHALLENGE 01</p><span class="status pending">NOT EVALUATED · PREPARATION 0.1</span><h1>Freeze the prediction before revealing the answer.</h1><p>The workflow is implemented and tested. The scientific challenge has <strong>not run</strong>: there is no frozen input package, preregistration, prediction or experimental comparison.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href={base+'protocol-paper.pdf'}>Read the protocol paper ↗</a><a href="#blockers">What still needs to happen ↓</a></div></header>
<section aria-labelledby="chronology"><h2 id="chronology">Actual chronology</h2><ol class="timeline">{state.phases.map((p,i)=><li><strong>{i+1}. {p.label}</strong><span>NOT OCCURRED</span></li>)}</ol><p class="subtle">These are pending scientific milestones, not animated progress or completed checklist items. Hashing the preparation download does not preregister an experiment.</p></section>
<section><h2>Selected candidate—not yet a frozen test series.</h2><p><strong>NASA TM-4074 / NACA 0012 experimental polar series.</strong> The archival experiment varies Mach, Reynolds number and transition treatment in the Langley low-turbulence pressure tunnel. Its documented ranges are source context, not production conditions.</p><p>The proposed prediction is a complete matched CL(α) and CD(α) series. That is more informative than one favorable scalar, but it is not a spatial field. Cp(x/c) availability is not claimed without a custodian checking the exact source.</p><div class="links"><a href={selection.candidate.url}>NASA source record ↗</a><a href={base+'selection.json'}>Selection rationale + exposure log</a></div><details><summary>Why this candidate, and what was deferred?</summary>{selection.candidates_considered.map(c=><p><strong>{c.name} — {c.decision}.</strong> {c.reason}</p>)}<p>NASA metadata confirms public access. Redistribution rights and the exact data extraction still need review; no source paper or experimental dataset is included in this release.</p></details></section>
<section class="boundary"><h2>A blindness limitation is already documented.</h2><p>The implementation task saw answer-bearing search snippets. It must not be reused as the blind predictor. A fresh runtime must receive only reviewed permitted inputs, with no inherited chat, RAG, browsing, reference mount or seal key.</p><p>A canonical benchmark may be present in model pretraining. The defensible claim is audited runtime reference withholding—not proof that a model has never encountered similar results.</p></section>
<section><div class="cards"><article><h2>What Aero may know</h2><p>Reviewed geometry, operating conditions, station locations, fluid properties, test-facility reconstruction and non-answer-bearing uncertainty information. Exact contents remain uncurated.</p></article><article><h2>What must stay sealed</h2><p>Measurements, coefficient curves, published CFD comparisons, author conclusions and modeling-choice outcomes. A separate custodian holds the encryption key outside predictor and repository access.</p></article></div></section>
<section><h2>Preregistered acceptance criteria</h2><span class="status pending">NOT FROZEN</span><p>The draft contains unresolved scientific fields. The framework refuses to freeze missing inputs or null thresholds. Proposed solver/model choices are not commitments.</p><p>Before production: select the exact experimental series, match transition and tunnel treatment, define three grid levels, wall/residual/conservation gates, comparison metrics and justified tolerances without viewing the answers.</p><a href={base+'preregistration.draft.json'}>Inspect the explicitly incomplete draft →</a><details><summary>Implemented comparison rules</summary><p>Absolute RMSE and maximum absolute error per registered quantity. Exact station matching, full-series coverage, no dropped points or post-unseal interpolation. Unknown uncertainty stays unknown; uncertainty overlap cannot retrospectively widen acceptance bounds. PASS, FAIL and MIXED are all supported. Failed numerical adequacy prevents an overall scientific PASS.</p></details></section>
<section><h2>Geometry, mesh, solver and numerical evidence</h2><p>No production artifacts exist. The prediction-freeze gate requires fourteen hashed evidence roles: requirements, first principles, geometry, topology, mesh, mesh diagnostics, deck, runtime, solver logs, residuals, conservation, wall diagnostics, grid study and extracted quantities.</p><p>The framework enforces sequencing and records reviewed isolation attestations. It does not itself secure or launch the Aero predictor/solver. A restricted execution adapter and actual supervisor evidence remain required.</p></section>
<section><h2>Frozen prediction → reference reveal → comparison</h2><p>None has occurred. An encrypted reference can only be unsealed after the frozen prediction and its retained evidence match a commit verified on origin/main. No result or comparison plot is substituted here.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Scientific commitment</th><th>SHA-256 / Git commit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Input / sealed reference</td><td>Not created</td></tr><tr><td>Preregistration</td><td>Not frozen or committed</td></tr><tr><td>Prediction freeze</td><td>Not created</td></tr><tr><td>Reference reveal / comparison</td><td>Not occurred</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Git anchoring provides inspectable history, not a trusted timestamp service or immutability against repository administrators. Custodian honesty and semantic input review remain separate requirements.</p></section>
<section id="blockers"><h2>What still needs to happen</h2><ol>{state.blockers.map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ol><p>Only after those steps: solve, freeze the complete prediction, publish its commitment, reveal the reference, compare automatically, and preserve the outcome—even if it fails.</p></section>
<section id="downloads"><h2>Reproduce the protocol implementation</h2><p>13 synthetic software tests pass, including a temporary Git-backed sequence. Those fixtures are explicitly not experimental measurements. The download contains code, tests, the draft, selection/exposure records and protocol paper. It does not contain a completed benchmark or hidden measurement package.</p><div class="links"><a class="primary" href={base+'preparation-sources.zip'}>Preparation source package ↓</a><a href={base+'protocol-paper.pdf'}>Protocol PDF ↗</a><a href={base+'README.md'}>Reproduction instructions</a><a href={base+'status.json'}>Status JSON</a><a href={base+'manifest.json'}>Preparation artifact hashes</a></div><p class="subtle">Scientific checkpoint hashes are absent by design. The preparation release has separate hashes for identity only. <a href="https://github.com/alexthegreat714/alex-blythe-site/commits/main/tools/aero-blind-validation">Implementation publication history ↗</a></p></section>
<section class="boundary"><h2>What this does—and does not—demonstrate</h2><p>This release demonstrates auditable protocol mechanics, not external validation. No PASS/FAIL/MIXED scientific result exists yet. A completed future benchmark can support only a bounded claim about the tested configuration and workflow, never universal Aero accuracy or design authority.</p></section>
